ps the problems I tackle can be up to 1000 dimensions, have up to 5000 data points.

More commonly I have 50 dimensions and 400 data points. Hence constructing K is a bottleneck.

I also use not just one gaussian process, but up to 500 independent gaussian processes, all of which contribute to a likelihood function which is used in MCMC.

I repeat this MCMC calculation maybe 50 times, it takes a few days for the whole process!

